<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-formo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to form</i> or <i>fashion
			beforehand</i>, <i>to instruct beforehand</i>, <i>to prepare</i>, etc. (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">his praeformat dictis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					7, 385</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">velut praeformata materia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					2, 6, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeformatae infantibus litterae,</span>”
				<i>traced beforehand</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					5, 14, 31</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
